{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ראשית דגנך", :translit "reshit deganekha", :gloss "the first of your grain"} {:he "משתמרת", :translit "mishtameres", :gloss "it is guarded / watched over"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ראשית דגנך", :b "משתמרת"}], :frame {:text "The phrase ראשית דגנך in Deuteronomy 18:4 is read as indicating that terumah from grain must be given from grain that has been watched over (משתמרת) — i.e., grain that was guarded from doubt regarding tithes or ritual impurity. The gematria equating ראשית דגנך with משתמרת signals that the 'first' obligated as a priestly gift must be from produce that was supervised and prepared accordingly.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 18:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "גז", :translit "gez", :gloss "shearing / fleece"} {:he "גז צאנך", :translit "gez tson'kha", :gloss "the shearings of your flock"} {:he "כמטר על גז", :translit "k'matar al gez", :gloss "like rain upon the fleece"} {:he "וראשית גז צאנך תתן לו", :translit "u'reshit gez tson'kha titen lo", :gloss "and the first of the shearings of your flock you shall give him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["גז צאנך" "כמטר על גז"]} {:kind :other, :note "Reading כמטר על גז (Proverbs 25:14) as 'like rain upon fleece' to teach that the gift of first shearings must be washed clean."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that the priestly gift of the first shearings must be given in a washed state, not still soiled. Proverbs 25:14 contains the phrase כמטר על גז, which Ba'al HaTurim reads as 'like rain upon the fleece,' indicating the fleece has been washed by rain — supporting the halakhic requirement that the gift be clean. The obligation appears in Deuteronomy 18:4: וראשית גז צאנך תתן לו.", :sources ["Chullin 136a" "Proverbs 25:14" "Deuteronomy 18:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ראשית דגנך", :a-value 988, :b "משתמרת", :b-value 1380, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["גז צאנך" "כמטר על